 are at hazardous sort of ranges for wildfire-related air pollution," with smoke exposure causing symptoms including coughing, throat irritation, and headaches [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;w6h4ZjWownUJIYopluGkPrc3EOxCdfSfcDP3_U8H_tcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyÛPhysicians and environmental health experts have highlighted that exposure to wildfire smoke can cause symptoms such as coughing, throat irritation, and headaches, even among high-level athletes [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Because athletes perform intense physical activity, their exposure to air pollutants is higher, which can pose risks to their long-term respiratory health [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;XFOq8_N77qIBxeCJhbEbVD2SAgeVs9FPLIKPpqHN3MMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;thRZOfgpYOttHRLiUAWNJj_OVkXxgneCEXInuJmokyYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;e-lu-PgzDtOKDABLWBb9c8UiBEEfujn15qsYrx2xoEEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxPconditions near the stadium remained in the unhealthy range as of Friday morningƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Zej1RD03nzqyZ06KCtsF8UMEBBxGySEyezZ1cTneF8gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxZconditions near the stadium remained in a moderate to unhealthy range as of Friday morningƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ris9xQf_vVY87ZgqrYVqRZVJkSsG_MUrqYWNWtPc8Goƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eU5wQHsf17UvcC_sCFItq_Omuz9stlaFSclkmWyQ-u8ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cLGmZf2UGZgz833ETKo4pITDc_sL0yPa_iX6QCEoZLAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyNicholas Watanabe, a professor of sport and entertainment management at the University of South Carolina, said that even if the final escapes the worst impacts, the close call "should serve as a wakeup call to FIFA and all other sport leagues and competitions of the need for regulations and a comprehensive plan to deal with climate risks" [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eMgymXffawQGNXHu80QioWDpLyzUUxvK7mcpXESHEm4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky…Until that day, the lack of a clear, disclosed plan from the tournament organizers leaves participants and observers to weigh the competing demands of athletic schedules and public health advisories [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesn't have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;A1tC4ul2j2S0VKHmvIqs5vRqIqAYgdLtozUmfRz2UgAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwreplace_exact_body_textƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GKaybxtxtDV4KoLZnt_PhSnHmkavnlxebYz2lbhoOmEƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;s0q94roJsykfYUjHCER3UIz6aJyNNWWST5jLIT1U1k4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxrepair_editorial_surfacesƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vRIzxTpmrh8eBWWvoLBLfa3awPVySKulpzjHNE2edd8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarklwriter-modelƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;o8VV1mosB9mTG3dr9ZnwRyDnvvpt3Sq3XqJsNLuZetUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyû## Source Audit

The manuscript draws exclusively from a single Grist article (grist.org, published 2026-07-17): "Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final. FIFA still doesn't have a plan." This is the sole current-provider source in the research packet, and the editorial risk flag `primary-source-unproven` applies: Grist is a secondary reporter whose piece itself relayed statements from the Associated Press, named academics, and named athletes. The manuscript is thus two removes from some of its most consequential claims, but the pipeline rules admit Grist as the source-bound evidentiary basis, and the factual claims it supports are adequate for a derivative summary piece of this length.

## Material Defects

**1. False attribution of original reporting (blocking).**
The body reads: "Requests for comment sent to FIFA regarding potential safety measures for players and fans went unanswered." No attribution is given â€” the grammar implies that this outlet's reporters sent those requests. The Grist source states explicitly: "Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment." The manuscript has laundered Grist's newsgathering action into a bare declarative that reads as this outlet's own reporting. This is a factual misrepresentation of editorial provenance and must be corrected by restoring the Grist attribution. The same sentence appears verbatim in the frontmatter description field, compounding the problem; `repair_editorial_surfaces` will regenerate the description from the corrected body.

**2. AQI range softened without source support (minor, correctable).**
The manuscript states "conditions near the stadium remained in a moderate to unhealthy range as of Friday morning." The source states "air quality near the stadium remained in the unhealthy range." Inserting "moderate to" introduces a qualifier that contradicts the source's more specific, worse-sounding figure. The repair restores the source's phrasing.

**3. Anonymous sourcing where named sources are available (specificity defect).**
The health-risks paragraph attributes claims to "physicians and environmental health experts" without naming anyone. The Grist source provides Dr. Courtney Howard â€” identified as an ER physician and Global Climate and Health Alliance official, quoted via the Associated Press â€” making a specific, quotable assertion about athletes practicing at hazardous AQI levels. Stripping the name in favour of a generic plural weakens attribution, obscures source motives, and makes the claim harder to verify. The repair reintroduces Dr. Howard's name and direct quote.

**4. Unsupported "long-term respiratory health" claim (overreach).**
The sentence "their exposure to air pollutants is higher, which can pose risks to their long-term respiratory health" extends beyond what the source asserts. The Grist article and Dr. Howard's AP quote address acute effects during activity and the immediate advisability of outdoor practice at hazardous AQI; neither makes a claim about long-term respiratory health outcomes. The repair removes this extension; Dr. Howard's direct quote covers the legitimate claim.

**5. Geographic imprecision (minor).**
The lede states the match will take place "this Sunday in New York City." The source says it is held "just outside of New York City." MetLife Stadium is in East Rutherford, New Jersey. While metro-area conventions often elide this distinction in casual usage, the source itself is explicit, and an accurate report should match it. The repair substitutes "just outside New York City."

**6. Vague closing abstraction (padding, specificity).**
The final sentence â€” "the lack of a clear, disclosed plan from the tournament organizers leaves participants and observers to weigh the competing demands of athletic schedules and public health advisories" â€” is a content-free abstraction. The source provides Nicholas Watanabe (University of South Carolina professor) with a named, direct closing statement about a "wakeup call" for FIFA and other leagues. Replacing the abstraction with the named quote eliminates padding, adds attribution, and satisfies the specificity requirement.

## Near-Duplicate Proximity Warnings

The deterministic standards system flagged 13 near-duplicate sentence pairs across all four body paragraphs. These reflect a genuine structural pattern: sentences within each paragraph share short topical phrases ("air quality," "smoke," "wildfire," "FIFA," "policy") because the prose restates the same facts with slightly varied language rather than advancing the argument. The bounded repairs above â€” replacing anonymous health sourcing with Dr. Howard's specific quote and replacing the vague closing with Watanabe's statement â€” will materially reduce repetition in paragraphs 3 and 4. Paragraphs 1 and 2 retain mild redundancy between sentence 1 (open-air stadium, uncertainty) and sentence 3 (AQI climbed Thursday, no contingency plan), and between the FIFA "no policy" sentence and the Grist non-response sentence. These remaining overlaps fall below blocking threshold given the single-source constraint: a 490-word piece covering one news event will naturally revisit its central fact. No additional repair is required for these.

## Fairness Note

The manuscript criticises FIFA for lacking an air quality policy. The source documents that Grist sought comment and FIFA did not respond. The source also records FIFA's previous statement: "Climate-related risks are assessed as part of overall tournament planning and managed in close coordination with host cities, stadium authorities, and national agencies." This is the closest available articulation of FIFA's position and is absent from the manuscript. Including it would strengthen fairness by representing the subject's stated framing even in the context of its silence on the specific question. This is a note rather than a blocking defect â€” the non-response is documented and attributed (to Grist after the repair), and the FIFA statement is from a prior exchange rather than a response to this specific crisis â€” but a future revision should consider including it.

## Pipeline Diagnosis

The source evidence is adequate and the assignment is grounded. The Grist article provides factual grounding for all core claims. Defects are writer-model artifacts: the false-attribution sentence, the AQI softening, the removal of named sources, the long-term claim extension, and the geographic imprecision are all introduced in the draft and absent from the source. All are bounded and correctable without source-layer replay.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DlXIAuTw54CWxfD0mYHV-5mDvinBFOv66LDwXrEuh3wƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ucy4lTvcge1C9dW-WFo6HNavHtAF87rI_7X48tvJJv4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx–Attribute 'requests for comment' to Grist, not this outlet â€” current phrasing falsely implies original newsgathering by the publishing organisation.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;936Q7bD-fBSHIrU-0_No-tNLWGO7wxWg6haQKOs_rqYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx£Correct AQI range description from 'moderate to unhealthy' to 'unhealthy' to match the source's precise statement about Friday-morning conditions near the stadium.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9qL4vW24imMDvgHiuHCKLLtxp-j45CDpRQQQaYYBQhcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyReplace anonymous 'physicians and environmental health experts' attribution with named Dr. Courtney Howard (ER physician, Global Climate and Health Alliance, quoted via AP) and remove the unsupported assertion about 'long-term respiratory health' risks that the source does not make.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;STQF_yvZg3o3M-y2b8tM3Esp518cx5d4AsdcEXQT44kƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx®Replace vague closing abstraction about 'competing demands' with Watanabe's specific named quote about this close call as a 'wakeup call to FIFA and all other sport leagues.'ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2uktNa2j9zGs3wfUun-Pjsjcnjn8aAu26HIB4NTX8Ioƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxÚCorrect stadium location from 'in New York City' to 'just outside New York City' to match the source, which explicitly says the match is held 'just outside of New York City' (MetLife Stadium is in East Rutherford, NJ).ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4cXKkcnlwwUHT5GfcTnNYhYXjnpOTxUHrHTlEGe_YRAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky$Five bounded repairs required: (1) remove false implication of original reporting on FIFA comment request; (2) correct "moderate to unhealthy" to match source's "unhealthy"; (3) replace anonymous health sourcing with named Dr. Courtney Howard and remove unsupported long-term claim; (4) replace vague closing sentence with Watanabe named quote; (5) correct stadium location from "in New York City" to "just outside New York City." Also regenerate editorial surfaces. Source evidence and assignment are sound; all defects are writer-model artifacts.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;kw9Z11qQUghE1tFTLPt461bv16HS12yTyaStvaZRK04ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwsubmit_revision_requestƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vF5Lin-4eUYYHvXh2DDJvwoyGHNFU1T9wY-ev1HD9lUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkgsuccessƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;LidQrZ3ulg2fPsWqMKFZznQ2260oUDHWbmIeAC78B3Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkicompletedƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;XPkSZh8ROC8DCEK7MnHXbL5xm-BWpObwfdY0qxwHX3sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkc162ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;j8jFqsppsMCBb-Qb4mb489EW9ckTCJp4b9aqWXo3pgUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkg0.29242ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0szWFC4KzcuxW_LuHn4EkvHrq3uqagGoWt_gbyPXvlcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf132059ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bi5GydciyxoEG9I2urKGOubXi8JARkHMqlBFLXUpWxEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd2054ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ORZJA0zYzE9UOW0t83l81bD5av5YtYfqlnAnOlDNVc4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkfresultƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;iqPTFE5aVZUHC5w9Y8LvRJKLrymLrgo-RqcI07ejZHMƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SXldZynxVmfNOlHpq5QRVc3tEduKjxCNl_IoA_wTo0Yƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;FvKBJCUDLBTgQOqWniq7yIyskT_2sDsXcsQjyGZiP3cƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke18363ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CCHi73mCXzfm4wFetL5EwQLI9BnSvIequEYFuoXY6jMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;_pMmB1wUt1ftBj_WAkrpf3Mi10PJyZ-zNKgKr3Qjatsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke18363ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IlJ1Mgd7ijY6N-W77JHrNtMaUJ