As the World Cup final approaches this Sunday in New York City, atmospheric conditions have cast uncertainty over the match, which is slated to be held in an open-air stadium [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Large swaths of the United States, including the Midwest and the East Coast, have been blanketed by smoke from Canadian wildfires, forcing cities to confront hazardous air quality [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While the air quality index in the region climbed to unhealthy levels on Thursday, triggering state alerts, the governing body for the tournament has not yet detailed a contingency plan for the event [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## A Gap in Institutional Preparedness

FIFA currently appears to have no standardized policy to implement adjustments or specific protocols for wildfire smoke, distinguishing it from other leagues that have already established such triggers [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). By contrast, the National Womenâ€™s Soccer League maintains a detailed policy that mandates game modifications or postponements when the air quality index reaches specific thresholds, such as 101 or 200 [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Requests for comment sent to FIFA regarding potential safety measures for players and fans went unanswered [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## Risks to Human Performance and Health

Physicians and environmental health experts have highlighted that exposure to wildfire smoke can cause symptoms such as coughing, throat irritation, and headaches, even among high-level athletes [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Because athletes perform intense physical activity, their exposure to air pollutants is higher, which can pose risks to their long-term respiratory health [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Vulnerable groups, including children, older individuals, and those with pre-existing conditions like asthma, also face increased dangers from the current air quality conditions [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).

## Watching the Atmosphere

Forecasters continue to track smoke patterns, with officials noting that conditions near the stadium remained in a moderate to unhealthy range as of Friday morning [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). While New York City has experienced hazy, orange skies throughout the week, the specific quality of the air on Sunday will depend on shifting wind patterns [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/). Until that day, the lack of a clear, disclosed plan from the tournament organizers leaves participants and observers to weigh the competing demands of athletic schedules and public health advisories [Wildfire smoke threatens the World Cup final, FIFA still doesnâ€™t have a plan](https://grist.org/extreme-weather/wildfire-smoke-threatens-the-world-cup-final-fifa-still-doesnt-have-a-plan/).
